IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P7-gates`

-- P7-sme: Articles 62 and 63 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744):
-- measures for providers and deployers, in particular SMEs, including start-ups (Art 62), and the derogation from the quality management system (Art 63).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Group `General`: Chapter VI applies from 2 August 2026.
-- Article 63(1) was replaced by the Omnibus: as enacted it spoke of microenterprises, as amended of SMEs, including start-ups. Both versions are encoded;
-- the dispatcher answers NOTHING before the group applies, so the as-enacted functions are tested directly (the group applies only from 2 August 2026,
-- after the Omnibus came into force on 27 July 2026).
-- Seam S12: the enterprise-size facts are plain BOOLEAN inputs named as the plan names them.
-- The text is the Publications Office consolidation of 27.7.2026, a rendering with no legal effect.

§ `Article 62: measures for providers and deployers, in particular SMEs, including start-ups`

-- src:981 | 1. Member States shall undertake the following actions:
@ref Art 62(1) lead (src:981)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the Member State undertakes the actions listed in points (a) to (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 62(1) the Member State has undertaken the actions listed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the Member State undertakes the actions listed in points (a) to (d)`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Member States shall undertake the following actions"

-- src:982 | (a) provide SMEs, including start-ups, having a registered office or a branch in the Union, with priority access to the AI regulatory sandboxes, to the extent that they fulfil the eligibility conditions and selection criteria; the priority access shall not preclude other SMEs, including start-ups, other than those referred to in this paragraph from access to the AI regulatory sandbox, provided that they also fulfil the eligibility conditions and selection criteria;
@ref Art 62(1)(a) first limb (src:982)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the enterprise is a micro, small or medium-sized enterprise as defined in Article 2 of the Annex to Recommendation 2003/361/EC` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enterprise has a registered office or a branch in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enterprise fulfils the eligibility conditions and selection criteria` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Member State provides the enterprise with priority access to the AI regulatory sandboxes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 62(1)(a) the Member State has provided the SME with priority access to the AI regulatory sandboxes` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT (`the enterprise is a micro, small or medium-sized enterprise as defined in Article 2 of the Annex to Recommendation 2003/361/EC` AND `the enterprise has a registered office or a branch in the Union` AND `the enterprise fulfils the eligibility conditions and selection criteria`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "SMEs, including start-ups, having a registered office or a branch in the Union ... to the extent that they fulfil the eligibility conditions and selection criteria"
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the Member State provides the enterprise with priority access to the AI regulatory sandboxes`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provide SMEs, including start-ups, having a registered office or a branch in the Union, with priority access to the AI regulatory sandboxes, to the extent that they fulfil the eligibility conditions and selection criteria"

-- src:982 | (a) provide SMEs, including start-ups, having a registered office or a branch in the Union, with priority access to the AI regulatory sandboxes, to the extent that they fulfil the eligibility conditions and selection criteria; the priority access shall not preclude other SMEs, including start-ups, other than those referred to in this paragraph from access to the AI regulatory sandbox, provided that they also fulfil the eligibility conditions and selection criteria;
@ref Art 62(1)(a) second limb (src:982)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the enterprise is an SME, including a start-up, other than one having a registered office or a branch in the Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enterprise is a micro, small or medium-sized enterprise as defined in Article 2 of the Annex to Recommendation 2003/361/EC` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enterprise fulfils the eligibility conditions and selection criteria` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 62(1)(a) the priority access precludes another SME from access to the AI regulatory sandbox` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        IF NOT (`the enterprise is an SME, including a start-up, other than one having a registered office or a branch in the Union`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "other SMEs, including start-ups, other than those referred to in this paragraph"
        IF `the enterprise is a micro, small or medium-sized enterprise as defined in Article 2 of the Annex to Recommendation 2003/361/EC` AND `the enterprise fulfils the eligibility conditions and selection criteria` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the priority access shall not preclude other SMEs, including start-ups, other than those referred to in this paragraph from access to the AI regulatory sandbox, provided that they also fulfil the eligibility conditions and selection criteria"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the provision speaks only of the case it names

-- src:983 | (b) organise specific awareness raising and training activities on the application of this Regulation tailored to the needs of SMEs including start-ups, deployers and, as appropriate, local public authorities;
