        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the provision speaks only of the case it names

-- src:997 | 2. Paragraph 1 of this Article shall not be interpreted as exempting those operators from fulfilling any other requirements or obligations laid down in this Regulation, including those established in Articles 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15, 72 and 73.
@ref Art 63(2) (the Articles the text names) (src:997)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the number of the Article of this Regulation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 63(2) the Article is one of those whose requirements or obligations paragraph 1 does not exempt the operator from fulfilling` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`Art 57 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter VI and Chapter VIII (group General) apply from the date Art 113 gives
        IF `the number of the Article of this Regulation` AT LEAST 9 AND `the number of the Article of this Regulation` AT MOST 15 THEN JUST TRUE  -- Articles 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15
        IF `the number of the Article of this Regulation` EQUALS 72 OR `the number of the Article of this Regulation` EQUALS 73 THEN JUST TRUE  -- Articles 72 and 73
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "any other requirements or obligations laid down in this Regulation, including those established in" names Articles and does not say that others are exempted
